# Data layer — cache, realtime, resume

Server state lives in TanStack Query v5, persisted to IndexedDB. Continuity
(instant paint on room re-entry, notification tap, cold launch) depends on the
rules below. Overview in [`docs/architecture.md`](../../docs/architecture.md).

## Never do this

- **No `useState` + `useEffect` fetching.** Add a `useQuery` hook in `src/api/`
 with a key from `queryKeys`. Per-mount fetch-and-discard is what made room
 re-entry feel clunky.
- **No refetch-on-realtime-event.** Merge `payload.new` into the cache with
 `setQueryData`. A full 100-row refetch per message is the old bug.
- **No `window.location.reload()` as a retry handler.** Use the `retry*` helpers
 in `src/api/cache.ts` — a reload throws away the warm cache.
- **No `window` custom events for invalidation** (`quacker:*-changed` is gone).
 Mutations call `invalidate*` from `src/api/cache.ts`.
- **Do not persist auth or one-shot queries.** Only keys whose root is in
 `PERSISTED_QUERY_ROOTS` are dehydrated.

## Conventions

| Concern | Where |
| --- | --- |
| Query keys | `src/api/queryKeys.ts` — add the root to `PERSISTED_QUERY_ROOTS` only if the data should survive a cold launch |
| Invalidation / retry | `src/api/cache.ts` |
| Realtime topic | Declare next to its row mapper in `src/api/*.ts`; subscribe with `useRealtimeTopic` |
| Message merge math | `src/api/messageSync.ts` — keep it dependency-free (vitest runs `environment: 'node'`) |
| Sends | `sendOrQueueMessage` from `src/lib/outbox/` — never call `addMessage` from a component |

- `asHookResult` maps `loading` → **`isPending`**, not `isFetching`. If you
 surface `isFetching` as loading, cached data flashes a skeleton on every
 revalidate and the whole point is lost.
- `error` is only surfaced when there is no data, so a failed background
 refetch shows stale data instead of an `ErrorState`.
- Realtime topics must be **stable values** (declared per `groupId`), and their
 handlers must close over the query client, not component state.

## Pitfalls found the hard way

- **`RealtimeTopic` circular imports.** Defining topics in a shared module
 while API modules import the type creates a cycle. Keep topic objects in the
 API module that owns the row mapper; keep only the type + hook in
 `src/lib/realtime/`.
- **StrictMode channel churn.** Double-invoked effects would remove a channel
 that is immediately resubscribed. The manager defers teardown by
 `TEARDOWN_DELAY_MS` and cancels it on resubscribe, and appends a generation
 counter to channel names so a pending async removal cannot collide.
- **Merging into an unresolved query is a no-op.** `applyMessageInsert` needs
 `getQueryData` to return an array; if the messages query is still pending
 there is nothing to merge into. In e2e, wait for the room to resolve (empty
 state or a message) before simulating a push.
- **Offline sends need their own retry.** `flushOutbox` on the `online` event is
 not enough — a transient failure right after reconnect otherwise strands the
 bubble in `sending…`. Retryable failures reschedule with backoff; permanent
 ones (RLS, malformed) mark the entry `failed` and show a Retry button.
- **Client-supplied message `id`.** The insert policy allows it, and it is what
 makes retries idempotent — a duplicate-key error on retry means success, not
 failure (`isDuplicateSendError`).
- **Sign-out must purge.** Query cache, persisted IndexedDB cache, outbox, and
  push inbox all get cleared on sign-out or user switch, and a `CACHE_OWNER_KEY`
  catches the case where a different user restores an old cache.
- **Restore must check owner + session.** `createIdbPersister().restoreClient`
  refuses to hydrate unless `CACHE_OWNER_KEY` matches `supabase.auth.getSession()`
  user id (missing owner → discard). `syncCacheOwner` purges on any mismatch,
  including `owner === null` with orphan IndexedDB. Outbox flush waits for
  `cacheOwnerReady` so a prior queue cannot run first.
- **Resume vs zombie channels.** OS can kill the Realtime socket while status
  stays `SUBSCRIBED`. On absence, `markRealtimeClosed()` before `refreshRealtime()`;
  if the socket is disconnected, `refreshRealtime` marks closed too. Coalesced
  wake-ups queue a follow-up pass (`pendingAbsenceMs`) instead of dropping.

## Service worker contract

`public/sw.js` and `supabase/functions/notify-new-message` are coupled: the push
payload carries the **full message row**. If you change the message shape,
update `PushedMessage` in `src/lib/notifications/pushInbox.ts` and the Edge
Function in the same change, then redeploy the function.

## Testing

- Pure logic (`messageSync`, `sendErrors`) → vitest, `src/**/*.test.ts`.
- Continuity behavior → `tests/e2e/offline-continuity.spec.ts` (in the
 `integration` Playwright project, needs Supabase). It covers cache re-entry
 with the network blocked, IndexedDB persistence, offline send + flush,
 missed-message recovery, push merge, in-app notification routing, and
 sign-out purge. Add `data-testid`s (`connection-status`, `message-pending`)
 for new chrome rather than role+name.
